& [Fault]
  + the first bookend dual-PowerShell replay found that the effect-wrapper manifest still retained the pre-bookend plan identity
  + the runner manifest had been rebuilt before the wrapper and producer manifests that also bind the changed navigation artifacts

& [Containment]
  + verification refused immediately on the first wrapper artifact mismatch before publication commit or push
  + no production permit CLI OpenSSH invocation EVO-X2 contact provider request remote call effect or live observation occurred

& [Resolution]
  + retain this fault in the runner evidence set and expand its artifact count
  + rebuild effect-wrapper then producer then runner evidence before recursive rehash and dual-PowerShell replay

& [Lesson]
  + every bookend navigation change must restart evidence formation from the oldest directly affected manifest rather than only the newest leaf
